{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the probabilities of obtaining a favorable outcome between the two lotteries and prefers the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome. In this decision problem, Lottery A offers a 50% chance of winning 1000 Euros and a 50% chance of 0 Euros, while Lottery B offers a 100% chance of winning 500 Euros. The outcomes are monetary, and a 'favorable outcome' can reasonably be interpreted as receiving a positive amount (i.e., any non-zero gain). Under this interpretation, Lottery A has a 50% probability of a favorable outcome, and Lottery B has a 100% probability. Thus, the decision reason can be applied, and it would prefer Lottery B due to its higher probability of yielding a favorable (non-zero) outcome.",
